    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["C12"],
      "pins": ["U4.4", "U4.5"],
      "nets": ["U4.C1P / U4.C1N (charge-pump stage 1 flying capacitor)"],
      "observed": "On the DISPLAY sheet (display.kicad_sch, page 5), C12 is connected across U4 pins 4 (C1P) and 5 (C1N) but its value is printed as '1m' (1 mF = 1000 µF), whereas its sibling flying capacitor C13 across pins 2/3 is correctly '1u'.",
      "expected": "The specification states 'C12 (1 µF) — across U4 C1P/C1N (charge-pump stage 1 flying capacitor)'. Both SSD1306 charge-pump flying capacitors must be 1 µF.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "C12 (1 µF) — across U4 C1P/C1N (charge-pump stage 1 flying capacitor)"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "display.kicad_sch (page 5): C12 drawn across U4 pins 4/5 with value '1m'; C13 across pins 2/3 with value '1u'"}
      ],
      "impact": "A 1000× oversized flying capacitor would not charge/discharge on the SSD1306 internal pump clock, preventing the charge pump from stepping VBAT up to the panel drive voltage; the OLED would fail to light (and a 1 mF part would not fit the small 0402/0603 footprint used for C13).",
      "confidence": 0.6
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The board otherwise matches the specification (NFC I2C pull-ups and FD line, display I2C strapping and data lines, TSC network, SWD header, decoupling, and the documented unresolved C18 '??'), but C12, the SSD1306 stage-1 charge-pump flying capacitor, is drawn as 1m instead of the specified 1 µF, which would break the display's internal voltage pump."
}

